# The ledge warning in the debug VS match on Battlefield: Link (player 1)
# against Mario (player 2), a human slot with no input, standing on the top
# platform. Link jumps from the middle of the main floor onto the left
# platform and dashes left to stand about two units short of its left end
# (-57.6), where the main floor lies below past the end, so the warning
# stays silent; a pause there logs his place through your position cue's
# stop line. Down drops him through onto the main floor, 12 units from its
# deadly left end (-68.4), and the left warning starts.
# Run from Git Bash with the debug match switches (31 is Battlefield), cues
# on:
#   MELEE_DEBUG_VS=1 MELEE_DEBUG_VS_STOCKS=2 MELEE_DEBUG_VS_STAGE=31 \
#     MELEE_A11Y_CUES=1 python tools/a11y/drive.py tools/a11y/match_ledge_battlefield.drive
# then grep -c '\[a11y\] cue ledge' build/drive/last.log prints 1: drive.py
# cannot fail on a line too many, which run_level.py checks itself.

# Start on the title screen goes straight into the debug match.
wait "state 0 scene 0$"
press Start until "boot scene: state \d+ scene 2$"

# Your cue starts at GO, Link standing in the middle under the top
# platform.
wait 'cue your position start pan 0\.00 pitch 0\.93 ' 60
sleep 1

# A jump left onto the left platform (y = 27.2, pitch 1.08), then a short
# dash left, which stops near the platform's end: x = -55.9 is pan -0.35.
press X+Left 300
sleep 1.2
press Left 150
sleep 1.2
press Start
wait 'cue your position stop pan -0\.3[3-6] pitch 1\.08 '
sleep 0.5
press Start
wait 'cue your position start '
sleep 1

# Down drops through: over the main floor near its left end, the warning
# starts as he falls, about 12 units from the end.
press Down 100
wait 'cue ledge left start pan -0\.([34]\d|50) pitch 1\.00 gain 0\.8\d interval 0\.200$' 5
sleep 1
